    <string name="src_after">Version after migration</string>
    <string name="pick_src_before">Pick the instance/folder for before</string>
    <string name="pick_src_after">Pick the instance/folder for after</string>
    <string name="plugin_hint">A plugin is a separately installed APK. Declaring a receiver for the agreed broadcast is enough to be discovered and invoked; the host needs no prior knowledge of the plugin\'s classes.</string>
    <string name="cfg_update_hint">Checks the repository releases once a day and notifies you when there is a new version. Downloading tries several mirrors in order and only falls back to the official link if all fail.</string>
    <string name="pick_launcher_hint">Claim your launcher from the list; its package name is then used to locate its data folder. Entries marked as suspected launcher are only guesses - trust your own judgement.</string>
    <string name="pick_launcher_search">Search by name or package</string>
    <string name="cfg_use_backend">Use backend (built-in CurseForge key, no need to apply for one)</string>
    <string name="cfg_use_backend_hint">The backend already has a CurseForge key, so you don\'t need your own while this is on. If you turn it off, fill in a key below or only Modrinth can be searched.</string>
    <string name="cfg_cf_key_hint">Fill in your own key when not using the backend (free from console.curseforge.com). Leave empty to use only Modrinth and the China mirror.</string>
    <string name="cfg_cf_route_title">Which route CurseForge takes</string>
    <string name="cfg_use_official_cf">Official direct (needs your own key)</string>
    <string name="cfg_cf_route_hint">These two are mutually exclusive: turning one on switches the other off automatically. Aggregate mode is unaffected - it queries both and merges results without duplicates.</string>
    <string name="cfg_copy_callback">Copy callback URL</string>
    <string name="cfg_gh_oauth">Open GitHub developer settings</string>
    <string name="cfg_callback_hint">The callback URL is built from the domain you visit, so whichever domain you use must be registered on GitHub. On a redirect_uri mismatch, open OAuth Apps and add the current domain to the callback list.</string>
    <string name="scan_launcher_dir_hint">Pick the top folder where your launcher keeps versions (usually instances or versions); it will drill down and find every version inside.</string>
